 A fractional `maxTimeout` rounds up to a whole millisecond. A `maxTimeout` of `0` schedules no timer, like `minTimeout: 0`. See the warning on `minTimeout`.
 
+##### Retry-After
+
+If the error thrown by an attempt has a numeric `retryAfter` (in seconds, finite and not negative), that time is waited **in addition to** the normal backoff delay, not instead of it. The backoff on top spreads out many clients that were all told to come back at the same moment. `maxTimeout` and `randomize` apply to the backoff only, and the total is still limited by `maxRetryTime`. Any other `retryAfter` value is ignored.
